Checking the schema export for the organizations table name and verifying that activity labels and event types are complete.

Confirmed the member.joined fan-out handles archived organizations correctly. Now checking other scheduled jobs and tasks that touch organizations, including overdue alerts, digests, usage counters, and trial downgrades.

Pending webhook deliveries should be marked failed rather than delivered. The retention sweep must leave its rows untouched. Search reindex is a background job and must also be guarded. Need to verify whether the scheduler iterates all organizations. The incrementUsage function should remain unchanged.

Usage listeners might still increment if events fire for deleted organizations, but that is out of scope. Pending webhook deliveries will be claimed and marked failed. Trial downgrades will skip silently when the organization is missing or archived.

The trial downgrade check must verify the organization exists before checking usage over-quota. This prevents incrementing failed trials when the organization is deleted or purged.

The search reindex job will check organization existence and archive status before indexing. Live organizations still proceed to indexIssue and related calls. The getPlanLimits call must remain before the loop.

Usage rollup must skip deleted organizations before calling recomputeUsage to avoid counting them as processed. The recomputeUsage service method will also guard against archived organizations, returning existing usage without rewriting it.

typescript
export async function recomputeUsage(orgId: OrgId): Promise<OrganizationUsage> {
  const org = await orgRepo.findOrgById(orgId);
  if (org && isArchived(org)) {
    return usageRepo.getUsage(orgId);
  }

  const usage = await usageRepo.recomputeUsage(orgId);
  if (!org) return usage;

Using `archivedAt !== null` directly avoids importing a soft-delete helper. The organizations table is already exported from the database schema, so `listOrgIdsForRollup` can import it alongside other tables.

The `listOrgIdsForRollup` query joins `organizationUsage` with `organizations`, filters out archived rows, and returns the oldest IDs first. The notification module will import `isArchived` from `@/lib/soft-delete`.

The notification module will return an empty recipient list when the organization is archived. The invitation acceptance handler will throw a NotFoundError for archived organizations and check revocation status.

The organization deletion service will import `isDeletedWorkspaceExpired` and `assertNotArchived`. It validates the confirmation slug and throws a `NotFoundError` if the organization is already archived.

The deletion service archives the organization and emits an `organization.deleted` event with the archived slug. It retains audit listeners during emission and releases them in a finally block. A new `restoreOrganization` function will look up the organization and throw a NotFoundError if it is missing.

The restore function validates the member and checks permissions before restoring. It emits an `organization.restored` event when the organization is actually archived.

The `retainOrganizationAuditListeners` export is confirmed. Importing it into the organization service creates no circular dependency with the activity service. The try/finally blocks for emitting events will remain inline rather than being extracted into a shared helper.

The digest builder will also guard against deleted workspaces, ensuring no digest is produced even if called directly. I need to verify whether any scheduler runs jobs independently of the rollup list, and confirm the search index job is on-demand only. I am checking that existing tests remain compatible: the permissions matrix iterates keys dynamically, so adding org:restore should not break it, and the activity action exhaustive switches already cover both new labels.

